-- title:
--   Gotzmann persistence over a base ring: I defines a Hilbert-functor point
-- statement:
--   Fix $n, m \in \mathbb{N}$ and a function $h : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}$ subject to three conditions: (1) $h(d) = \binom{n+d}{n}$ for all $d < m$; (2) for every $e \ge m$, every field $K$ and every ideal $J$ of $K[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ that is the span of a set of forms of degree $e$, if $\dim_K \mathrm{piece}(J,e) = h(e)$ then $\dim_K \mathrm{piece}(J,e+1) \le h(e+1)$; and (3) for every $e \ge m$ there are a field $K$ and such an ideal $J$ generated by forms of degree $e$ with $\dim_K \mathrm{piece}(J,e) = h(e)$ and $\dim_K \mathrm{piece}(J,e+1) = h(e+1)$. Here `piece J d` denotes the $d$-th graded piece of the quotient, namely the space of degree-$d$ forms modulo those lying in $J$. Let $A$ be a commutative ring and $I$ an ideal of $A[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ which is the span of a set of forms of degree $m$, and assume that `piece I m` is a projective $A$-module whose rank at every point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$ equals $h(m)$, and likewise that `piece I (m+1)` is projective with rank $h(m+1)$ at every point. Then there is a term of `Point A n h` whose underlying ideal is $I$: that is, $I$ is stable under taking homogeneous components, and for every $d$ the $A$-module `piece I d` is finite, projective, and of rank $h(d)$ at every point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$.
--
--   This is a base-ring form of Gotzmann's persistence theorem: the maximal-growth conditions (2) and (3) on $h$ in degrees $\ge m$ propagate projectivity and constancy of ranks of the graded pieces from degrees $m$, $m+1$ to all degrees, so that an ideal generated in degree $m$ with the expected ranks is an $A$-valued point of the Hilbert functor attached to $h$. It is used in the construction of the scheme representing that functor and the closed immersion of it into a projective space.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_HilbertFunctor_exists_point_I_eq_of_projective_piece_succ.lean

